& [SemanticSubjectAudit] passes
  + the committed subject is exactly the existing ordered TopologyEntryObservation sequence plus its count and encoding domain
  + every public M2A observation and stream semantic field is included
  + assembly limits, deadline, policy syntax, correlation identities, carrier profiles, and proof lineage are excluded for the explicit reason that they are not scanner inventory-record content
  + exclusion from digest subject does not discard lineage because the complete assembly is retained in the output-only result
  + the proposed digest can later be supplied to receipt logic only through separate physical, repeat-inventory, and issuance authority
  - never: promote this supplied commitment directly to TopologyReceipt.ordered_inventory_sha256 proof

& [AmbiguityAudit] passes subject to canonical restatement
  + the zero-terminated ASCII domain is self-delimiting before a fixed-width entry count
  + all unsigned integers have fixed big-endian width
  + every enum has an explicit closed one-byte tag independent of Rust and serde
  + option presence, text length, sequence count, entry start, stream start, and field tags remove concatenation ambiguity
  + file identity and SHA-256 hex strings have exact validated decoded byte widths
  + field order is source-declared and can be repeated verbatim in canonical authority
  + tag values overlap only across structurally delimited namespaces and cannot alias another valid parse
  + no locale, path rewrite, Unicode normalization, native layout, Debug, or serializer output participates

& [DataDesignAudit] passes
  + conceptual subject is an ordered inventory observation sequence
  + logical representation is one domain, one count, and repeated tagged field tuples
  + physical representation is an incremental SHA-256 input stream, not a persisted canonical-byte file
  + lineage representation is a private output-only wrapper retaining the entire assembly beside the digest
  + authority representation remains supplied_structurally_closed_ordered_inventory_commitment only
  + compatibility is profile exact with no implicit migration or default

& [ImplementationFeasibility] is dependency ready
  + cantor_ecosystem already has workspace sha2 available and locked; no new dependency or Cargo delta is needed
  + WindowsSuppliedTopologyInventoryAssembly exposes immutable ordered members, entry_count, total_file_bytes, and plan
  + each closed member exposes its TopologyEntryObservation while retaining its complete carrier
  + TopologyEntryObservation and nested values expose every required field to safe Rust
  + fixed arrays and direct slice updates satisfy the no-whole-inventory-allocation rule
  + implementation should use the existing sha2 API directly; extracting or widening the prior private accumulator is unnecessary unless canonical SJS finds a proven reduction
  + zero unsafe and zero platform or filesystem calls are sufficient

& [ConstraintAudit] identifies canonical obligations
  + restate exact tag table and field order without abbreviation
  + distinguish encoding profile from result profile and require both exact
  + bind the source and all three prerequisite hashes and signatures
  + specify checked usize-to-u64 count conversion and checked byte-total recomputation
  + specify lowercase output hex independent of serde
  + require at least one independently computed reference vector and perturbation vectors for every field class
  + prohibit accepting a digest, raw observation sequence, or reconstructed assembly as success input
  + prohibit claims of physical origin, completeness, freshness, equality between scans, atomicity, receipt, or admission

& [RiskAudit] is bounded
  + [highest_risk] a stable-looking digest could be rhetorically inflated into physical inventory proof
  + [second_risk] implementation could hash JSON or omit a field while appearing deterministic
  + [third_risk] policy or proof-lineage fields could leak into the inventory subject and make future receipt semantics unstable
  + [fourth_risk] whole-inventory buffering could violate resource intent despite valid output
  + exact canonical grammar, retained lineage, negative static checks, reference vectors, and evidence-grade naming address these risks

& [EffectAudit] passes
  + required implementation is deterministic in-memory validation and hashing only
  + filesystem, Windows, handle, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, Git, model, tool, fixture, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, and promotion authority remain absent
  + physical scanning and all previously locked effect paths remain locked

